>In article <1989Aug10.022252.24080@tmsoft.uucp> mshiels@tmsoft.UUCP (Michael A. Shiels) writes:
>>I too just compiled nethack 3.0 under MSC 5.1 without too many problems.  
>>Only one thing I can find funny is every once in a while a 'H' is left on
>>the screen from the cursor motion string.  When I use the <ESC>[...f string
>>little 'f's are left all over?  HELP!!
The bug is in the posted version of tgoto.c; it doesn't nul-terminate
the returned string.  The fix is trivial; add the line
*out = '\0' just before the return in tgoto.c.

Recompile and it works fine.


